messages:
Jules (AE): Hey team — Zenith is asking for a performance POC next week. Goal: validate sustained 100 RPS with 2k-token avg payload, 99th percentile generation latency <= 350ms, and a short burst to 300 RPS for 2m. Can SRE + Infra + Sales-Eng align on test plan, runbook, and any enterprise blockers?

Aditi (SRE): I can own the load run. Suggest: smoke (10m), step ramp to 100 RPS (10m), soak 60m, then 2m burst to 300 RPS. We should capture p50/p95/p99, success rate, and tail token counts.

Anya (Sales-Eng): Also they'll want cost estimate and how we handle bursts vs reserved capacity. I can draft the pricing blurb but need expected GPU footprint / concurrency.

Mike (Infra): To hit 100 RPS at ~2k tokens we should enable prefix KV caching and set batch_size=4 for generation to reduce per-token overhead. If we use an fp16-quantized variant we can halve mem and increase concurrency.

Aditi (SRE): Quick k6 snippet I plan to use (ramp + constant):
```js
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';
export let options = { stages: [ { duration: '10m', target: 100 }, { duration: '60m', target: 100 }, { duration: '2m', target: 300 }, { duration: '5m', target: 0 } ] };
export default function () {
  let payload = JSON.stringify({ input: '... ~2000 tokens sample...' });
  let res = http.post('https://api.redwood.example/v1/generate', payload, { headers: { 'Authorization': 'Bearer $POC_KEY', 'Content-Type': 'application/json' } });
  sleep(1);
}
```

Jules (AE): Nice. Zenith also completed the security questionnaire — they flagged encryption in transit, KMS separation, and audit logs. Clare, can you confirm our answers are still valid for a POC?

Clare (Security): For POC we can provide TLS + customer-managed KMS for model keys, plus VPC peering to keep traffic off public internet. Audit logs: we retain request metadata for 30 days by default; can extend to 90d on request. We need a signed NDA before exchanging any sensitive prompt sets.

Anya (Sales-Eng): Pricing note: for a one-week POC with that load profile, rough hosted burn estimate = ~2 GPU-days if we use quantized rtx-class instances; reserved capacity quote (monthly commit) would be about 3x the hourly cost for that peak. I can give a firm number after Mike confirms the GPU type.

Mike (Infra): Tentative infra plan: 2x A10-equivalent nodes for baseline 100 RPS with batching; add 1-2 nodes to cover the 300 RPS burst depending on GPU choice. I'll validate exact VM types and expected token/sec tonight.

Aditi (SRE): Runbook checklist I'm adding: 1) Validate sample prompts and tokenization matches prod; 2) Set telemetry (Prometheus + traces) and enable token-level cost export; 3) Pre-warm model and KV cache 15m before soak; 4) Activate circuit-breaker to fail open to smaller variant if p99 > 600ms.

Jules (AE): Perfect. Action items: Mike — confirm node types and expected token/sec by EOD. Aditi — prepare k6 artifacts and dashboards. Clare — finalize POC security answers and NDA text. Anya — draft pricing note to Zenith. I'll schedule the run for next Tuesday at 09:00 PT pending confirmations. :calendar:

zenith-poc-bot: Reminder queued: generate POC creds and ephemeral key pair when NDA signed.

Anya (Sales-Eng): One more ask from their infra team — can we provide per-route latency histograms and a sample trace for a 2k-token request? They want to validate end-to-end timings.

Aditi (SRE): Yes — we'll export Jaeger traces with service spans for gateway, model runtime, and tokenization. I'll attach an example trace after the smoke run.

Jules (AE): Great, thanks everyone. If any blocker pops up call it out here asap. :thumbsup:
